[[:db/retract 17592186177249 :answer-field/choices 17592186177252] [:db/retract 17592186177249 :answer-field/choices 17592186177254] [:db/retract 17592186177255 :answer-field/choices 17592186177258] [:db/retract 17592186177255 :answer-field/choices 17592186177259] [:db/retract 17592186177255 :answer-field/choices 17592186177260] {:db/id 17592186179700 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cdfbed1a-906b-56f6-99dc-ee6b37df7069" "question-53cf2acb-145a-5506-896e-6068ff12e934" "question-00627a83-5d8e-5013-8a9c-ba462e57258b" "question-118e7fad-b51e-5b1f-8cd6-2d517d8a5df9" "question-1e29b1c7-106c-5ab0-8d9e-819610a3356d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179562 :question/problem "Find the value of $\\dfrac{5}{12} - \\dfrac{11}{12}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{12} - \\dfrac{11}{12} = \\dfrac{5 - 11}{12}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $5 - 11$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/d9/d9367da101187cf8861458e58f16ea179cff66477d1b9060d3ae199ff8bb3843.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5 - 11}{12} = \\dfrac{-6}{12} = -\\dfrac{6}{12}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{6}{12} = -\\dfrac{6 \\div 6}{12 \\div 6} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{12} - \\dfrac{11}{12} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179697 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8d8f39de-a2f7-5903-8fdc-c4a3db5001e2" "question-9177f11e-16b2-5f25-b1c3-d0c370d0a589" "question-a6a01cd3-8e80-578c-a68c-ccfe0c02910d" "question-39ba11e1-e910-5353-9445-994f4bc57a7d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179559 :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{5}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ as $\\dfrac{2}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{6} - \\dfrac{5}{6} = \\dfrac{2 - 5}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2 - 5$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/c6/c63a3db44b79e751c7cf1a49dcebcbb1d00cea0427da4ef271d07646e4be2748.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2 - 5}{6} = \\dfrac{-3}{6} = -\\dfrac{3}{6}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{3}{6} = -\\dfrac{3 \\div 3}{6 \\div 3} =-\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{5}{6} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179698 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c7de1d22-ba4a-5f8e-8822-f3f4dfdb810b" "question-3d3c4be6-4f0d-589b-961f-38e5107411d1" "question-bfb8f280-e1d8-5d03-9404-6aac25e66c3a" "question-b3cacdef-dab0-554e-ba7e-6bcb902467ae"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179560 :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\dfrac{1}{4} - \\dfrac{5}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ as $\\dfrac{3}{12}$ and $\\dfrac{5}{6}$ as $\\dfrac{10}{12},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{12} - \\dfrac{10}{12} = \\dfrac{3 - 10}{12}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $3 - 10$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/f4/f4dc7569aa731c13cf150d867479704cc46cbf7d6502cda4100538b4b2a7e9dc.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3 - 10}{12} = \\dfrac{-7}{12} = -\\dfrac{7}{12}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-841f7692-e519-5922-bdbc-38496ec5b53f" "question-38a15d99-3414-508c-84b1-39ed573baedb" "question-1599934d-a927-5358-9a1f-a60248bbf5f8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179561 :question/problem "Find the value of $\\dfrac{1}{3} - 2\\,\\dfrac{2}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $2 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2 \\,\\dfrac{2}{3} = \\dfrac{(2 \\times 3) + 2}{3} = \\dfrac{8}{3}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{8}{3} = \\dfrac{1 - 8}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $1 - 8$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/74/74047d21ae2b703b9962b9655eacbe2eee1a8d94fa4fd36a2924a6b02601d4fa.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1 - 8}{3} = \\dfrac{-7}{3} = -\\dfrac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{7}{3} = -2 \\, \\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-cdfbed1a-906b-56f6-99dc-ee6b37df7069" :question/id #uuid "cdfbed1a-906b-56f6-99dc-ee6b37df7069" :question/math-academy-id "q-101209" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{9}-\\frac{7}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{9}-\\frac{7}{9}=\\frac{2-7}{9}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/bb/bb81cb03e8205a9df3a62ed47ca7b2a4c1a66ad990eaf248f8701480bb2d5bb1.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{2-7}{9}=\\frac{-5}{9}=-\\frac{5}{9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ed07ce1b-2e1b-5fc8-98af-e62943422cd9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ed07ce1b-2e1b-5fc8-98af-e62943422cd9" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed07ce1b-2e1b-5fc8-98af-e62943422cd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eb8c6b69-277e-56f8-9e05-a7336aec36da" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cf2e7900-20db-5d61-9b09-d574171ca258" "answer-eb8c6b69-277e-56f8-9e05-a7336aec36da" "answer-0bc4f8fd-ffd1-5e06-a562-5ecb24dab1d4" "answer-0c063043-348e-5eac-84ed-a7672540af64" "answer-1b4bc9a3-a0f7-576d-b858-9fdbfa22c852"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf2e7900-20db-5d61-9b09-d574171ca258" :answer/id #uuid "cf2e7900-20db-5d61-9b09-d574171ca258" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb8c6b69-277e-56f8-9e05-a7336aec36da" :answer/id #uuid "eb8c6b69-277e-56f8-9e05-a7336aec36da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{9}" :