ion.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-89775857-af06-5122-a629-260ef3b33e00"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-89775857-af06-5122-a629-260ef3b33e00" :answer-field/id #uuid "89775857-af06-5122-a629-260ef3b33e00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d8564b0f-dc6f-53da-bb88-09c871d92f9c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b3ba7c0d-a9b6-5bce-89b2-f81ddd81c18d" "answer-dce90268-d28d-57c3-a229-3c3255e2afbf" "answer-c42d8bbf-060e-5bec-9047-045c39110d97" "answer-a8d71d55-26d9-5246-acf4-1fa4aba22737" "answer-d8564b0f-dc6f-53da-bb88-09c871d92f9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3ba7c0d-a9b6-5bce-89b2-f81ddd81c18d" :answer/id #uuid "b3ba7c0d-a9b6-5bce-89b2-f81ddd81c18d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dce90268-d28d-57c3-a229-3c3255e2afbf" :answer/id #uuid "dce90268-d28d-57c3-a229-3c3255e2afbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c42d8bbf-060e-5bec-9047-045c39110d97" :answer/id #uuid "c42d8bbf-060e-5bec-9047-045c39110d97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8d71d55-26d9-5246-acf4-1fa4aba22737" :answer/id #uuid "a8d71d55-26d9-5246-acf4-1fa4aba22737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8564b0f-dc6f-53da-bb88-09c871d92f9c" :answer/id #uuid "d8564b0f-dc6f-53da-bb88-09c871d92f9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179934 :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{3}{8}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write $\\frac{1}{6}$ as $\\frac{4}{24}$ and $\\frac{3}{8}$ as $\\frac{9}{24},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{24}-\\frac{9}{24}=\\frac{4-9}{24}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-9$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/3f/3f5b60548cfd0332c74508678de51481f9fa149466c7d7880217b905e4d3891a.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-9}{24}=\\frac{-5}{24}=-\\frac{5}{24}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177273 :answer-field/correct 17592186177276 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-841f7692-e519-5922-bdbc-38496ec5b53f" :question/id #uuid "841f7692-e519-5922-bdbc-38496ec5b53f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119552" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{1}{5}-1\\,\\frac{3}{10}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{3}{10}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{(1\\times 10)+3}{10}=\\frac{13}{10}\n$$\n\nAlso, we write $-\\frac{1}{5}$ as $-\\frac{2}{10}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{10}-\\frac{13}{10}=\\frac{-2-13}{10}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-2-13$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/65/651e46f49551c462bbf15db5e1fc554aa0ff81d7f81fc64286f15c226be69800.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2-13}{10}=\\frac{-15}{10}=-\\frac{15}{10}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{15}{10}=-\\frac{15÷5}{10÷5}=-\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}=-1\\,\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-49500cf1-dfa6-5c93-8a4f-7807a818ec19"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-49500cf1-dfa6-5c93-8a4f-7807a818ec19" :answer-field/id #uuid "49500cf1-dfa6-5c93-8a4f-7807a818ec19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3fa215d3-0b57-54ce-a8c7-ad8f3fa77766" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3fa215d3-0b57-54ce-a8c7-ad8f3fa77766" "answer-115b8fee-d484-5ba9-846e-26fb6bd010a9" "answer-b05dacd2-7d24-591a-b1c9-f9fd71bb8f32" "answer-a99e9b36-96e1-51c0-b0ef-9aa47284dd5b" "answer-564f7a03-8298-555e-9435-e9cc345d01e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fa215d3-0b57-54ce-a8c7-ad8f3fa77766" :answer/id #uuid "3fa215d3-0b57-54ce-a8c7-ad8f3fa77766" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-115b8fee-d484-5ba9-846e-26fb6bd010a9" :answer/id #uuid "115b8fee-d484-5ba9-846e-26fb6bd010a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b05dacd2-7d24-591a-b1c9-f9fd71bb8f32" :answer/id #uuid "b05dacd2-7d24-591a-b1c9-f9fd71bb8f32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a99e9b36-96e1-51c0-b0ef-9aa47284dd5b" :answer/id #uuid "a99e9b36-96e1-51c0-b0ef-9aa47284dd5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-564f7a03-8298-555e-9435-e9cc345d01e6" :answer/id #uuid "564f7a03-8298-555e-9435-e9cc345d01e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-38a15d99-3414-508c-84b1-39ed573baedb" :question/id #uuid "38a15d99-3414-508c-84b1-39ed573baedb" :question/math-academy-id "q-119559" :question/problem "Determine the value of $2\\,\\frac{3}{4}-3\\,\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $2\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{(2\\times 4)+3}{4}=\\frac{11}{4}\n$$\n\nWe also write $3\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{(3\\times 4)+1}{4}=\\frac{13}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our problem now is to work out the following:\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{4}-\\frac{13}{4}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{4}-\\frac{13}{4}=\\frac{11-13}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $11-13$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/be/befeb1f1947d5325530ac772fcf1411b04ae74bd78e377dc3eff547461a87627.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{11-13}{4}=\\frac{-2}{4}=-\\frac{2}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{4}=-\\frac{2÷2}{4÷2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7f80531f-0b35-5d8e-b16e-de1b40fdee65"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7f80531f-0b35-5d8e-b16e-de1b40fdee65" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f80531f-0b35-5d8e-b16e-de1b40fdee65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-83330878-3a8f-572f-8fa3-39627f40a480" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4c6f55f6-aa95-5757-97d1-fea7904befd7" "answer-e97aadf7-8654-534c-ba18-ede197cda907" "answer-83330878-3a8f-572f-8fa3-39627f40a480" "answer-56135516-4bbe-5149-8994-ebb28c6fa458" "answer-67247274-c78a-5954-a1b1-95cb4632266e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c6f55f6-aa95-5757-97d1-fea7904befd7" :answer/id #uuid "4c6f55f6-aa95-5757-97d1-fea7904befd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e97aadf7-8654-534c-ba18-ede197cda907" :answer/id #uuid "e97aadf7-8654-534c-ba18-ede197cda907" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83330878-3a8f-572f-8fa3-39627f40a480" :answer/id #uuid "83330878-3a8f-572f-8fa3-39627f40a480" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56135516-4bbe-5149-8994-ebb28c6fa458" :answer/id #uuid "56135516-4bbe-5149-8994-ebb28c6fa458" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67247274-c78a-5954-a1b1-95cb4632266e" :answer/id #uuid "67247274-c78a-5954-a1b1-95cb4632266e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179930 :question/problem "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{5}-1\\,\\frac{1}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{(1\\times 5)+1}{5}=\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{6}{5}=\\frac{2-6}{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-6$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/ed/ed6c51ffa37fa80ca17575c241738c602cb81cb2bca500fea1fb3231063763b2.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{2-6}{5}=\\frac{-4}{5}=-\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177249 :answer-field/correct 17592186177250 :answer-field/choices ["answer-684780d2-2c9c-5628-88dd-65e3f2a4915e" "answer-2b8f5c6f-df95-5cfb-9550-a83a1314f99a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-684780d2-2c9c-5628-88dd-65e3f2a4915e" :answer/id #uuid "684780d2-2c9c-5628-88dd-65e3f2a4915e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b8f5c6f-df95-5cfb-9550-a83a1314f99a" :answer/id #uuid "2b8f5c6f-df95-5cfb-9550-a83a1314f99a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1599934d-a927-5358-9a1f-a60248bbf5f8" :question/id #uuid "1599934d-a927-5358-9a1f-a60248bbf5f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119549" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{1}{3}-1\\,\\frac{1}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{9}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{(1\\times 9)+1}{9}=\\frac{10}{9}\n$$\n\nAlso, we write $-\\frac{1}{3}$ as $-\\frac{3}{9}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{9}-\\frac{10}{9}=\\frac{-3-10}{9}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-3-10$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/f2/f27b92c1bbd62f5cba5fc75a4205034a24fb0298e77a662d6c59203dd42a2760.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-3-10}{9}=\\frac{-13}{9}=-\\frac{13}{9}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{13}{9}=-1\\,\\frac{4}{9}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-06b7d979-b715-582b-b778-9506c304818f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06b7d979-b715-582b-b778-9506c304818f" :answer-field/id #uuid "06b7d979-b715-582b-b778-9506c304818f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-784d6498-f8d8-591b-8aaf-6809b37ed91a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-10c778ac-45a7-5054-9e7a-d2aca2969d45" "answer-784d6498-f8d8-591b-8aaf-6809b37ed91a" "answer-ceff5ae7-fcad-552c-a144-b19ffb515812" "answer-1132f49f-3789-5224-9661-f88d99141500" "answer-cce9891f-2dd1-562f-94b2-7ff3b5e22bc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10c778ac-45a7-5054-9e7a-d2aca2969d45" :answer/id #uuid "10c778ac-45a7-5054-9e7a-d2aca2969d45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-784d6498-f8d8-591b-8aaf-6809b37ed91a" :answer/id #uuid "784d6498-f8d8-591b-8aaf-6809b37ed91a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ceff5ae7-fcad-552c-a144-b19ffb515812" :answer/id #uuid "ceff5ae7-fcad-552c-a144-b19ffb515812" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1132f49f-3789-5224-9661-f88d99141500" :answer/id #uuid "1132f49f-3789-5224-9661-f88d99141500" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cce9891f-2dd1-562f-94b2-7ff3b5e22bc4" :answer/id #uuid "cce9891f-2dd1-562f-94b2-7ff3b5e22bc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179931 :question/problem "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{2}{3}-1\\frac{5}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{5}{6}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{(1\\times 6)+5}{6}=\\frac{11}{6}\n$$\n\nAlso, we write $-\\frac{2}{3}$ as $-\\frac{4}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{4}{6}-\\frac{11}{6}=\\frac{-4-11}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-4-11$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/69/69aec22c2950768abf58a2cae84d3b90a52c79ad44e60d0008605feca272357e.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-4-11}{6}=\\frac{-15}{6}=-\\frac{15}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{15}{6}=-\\frac{15÷3}{6÷3}=-\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{5}{2}=-2\\,\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177255 :answer-field/correct "answer-e6e81049-86ab-5d8c-b6c4-344a018e1375" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b8e0f802-017d-573f-8d26-6bcba6dddf07" "answer-478602a6-4124-5195-96b1-d9ffad534b57" "answer-e6e81049-86ab-5d8c-b6c4-344a018e1375"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8e0f802-017d-573f-8d26-6bcba6dddf07" :answer/id #uuid "b8e0f802-017d-573f-8d26-6bcba6dddf07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-478602a6-4124-5195-96b1-d9ffad534b57" :answer/id #uuid "478602a6-4124-5195-96b1-d9ffad534b57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6e81049-86ab-5d8c-b6c4-344a018e1375" :answer/id #uuid "e6e81049-86ab-5d8c-b6c4-344a018e1375" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180667 :tutorial/content "How can we subtract fractions, like $\\dfrac{2}{4} - \\dfrac{5}{4}?$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominator ($4$), we can combine them into one fraction.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{4}-\\frac{5}{4} & =\\frac{2-5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-5$ using our number line:\n\n![](images/c6/c63a3db44b79e751c7cf1a49dcebcbb1d00cea0427da4ef271d07646e4be2748.png)\n\nWe get $2-5=-3,$ and therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2-5}{4}=\\frac{-3}{4}=-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** If two fractions have different denominators, we need to put them over a common denominator *first* and *then* subtract!" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179835 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
